abstract: >
  AetherProof is a formal architecture for specification-driven proof
  construction, incremental differential proving, and counterexample-guided
  remediation in multi-agent software ecosystems. It is the verification
  layer of the Aether family, above AetherGit (storage) and AetherFlow
  (integration). The paper specifies three functional layers (TLA+,
  Why3/Lean, SMT-LIB/Z3), a Canonical Specification Representation (CSR)
  with three distinct identities, a Proof Dependency Graph (PDG), and a
  counterexample-guided remediation protocol. No implementation is built
  and no empirical evaluation is performed.
